 
 = Reed Lamp = 
 
 The reed lamp is an invented lamp made for this test file . A thin reed holds the wick , and the oil sits in a clay bowl below it . 
 
 = = Use = = 
 
 Farmers in a pretend valley light the reed lamp at dusk and carry it to the barn . The lamp burns for three hours on one bowl of oil . 
 
 = Zqjx = 
 
 Zqjx is the name of a small grey bird in a tale written for this file . It sings two notes at dawn , and children in the tale call every grey bird Zqjx after it . 
 
 = = Song = = 
 
 Old people say that Zqjx learned its song from the wind . A farmer who hears Zqjx at noon will have rain by evening , and a child who sees Zqjx first in spring keeps a feather in a tin . 
 
 = Stone Mill = 
 
 The Stone Mill is an old water mill on a stream that is only imagined . Its wheel turns all year , and the miller grinds wheat , rye and oats on the lower floor . 
 
 = = Bells = = 
 
 A bell rings when the grain runs low ; the miller then pours more grain into the hopper above the stones . 
 
 = Green Market = 
 
 The Green Market is a weekly market held in a yard of the pretend town . Traders bring apples , honey , candles , woollen hats and painted pots , and a fiddler plays by the well until the bells ring for supper . 
 
 = = History = = 
 
 The market began when two brothers set up a table of pears under an elm tree . Within ten years there were forty stalls , and the town council paved the yard with river stones . 
 
